# SystemC/TLM testbench quality (no coverage shortcuts)

Apply whenever creating or editing a SystemC/TLM2.0 testbench, `*_tb.cpp`,
`*_test*.cpp`, `run_tests.sh`, or coverage filler. Complements
`test-coverage-asan` (95% + ASan) and `new-ip-ci-checklist` (CI wiring).
**Line coverage is not evidence.** Do not add a case whose only job is to
execute a branch.

## Fail closed (harness)

- Every compiled suite/binary must be **called** in Release, `--asan`, and
  `--coverage`. Do not compile FUNC023 then skip it in `run_tests()`.
- Propagate every child exit. Never `|| true`, ignore `RUN_EXIT`,
  `quick_exit(0)`, or treat timeout as PASS.
- `sc_stop()` / `SC_REPORT_*` failures must increment a fail counter and
  fail `sc_main`. Do not demote ERROR to WARN to stay green.
- Coverage must not continue after a failed semantic run.

## Frontdoor first

Drive production sockets, ports, and CSRs via `b_transport` / bound signals.
Do **not** count as IP conformance:

- `#define private public`, `friend` testbench, `const_cast` of `const` DUT state
- Direct calls to private methods, register callbacks, or engine threads
- `inject_*` / `dbg_*` / `load_*` / `force_*` as the **only** stimulus
- Mock harness that implements the DUT port itself (e.g. fake EDN endpoint)

Helpers/backdoors may exist as **labeled** unit tests; they do not replace a
frontdoor case for the same path.

## Independent oracle

Every case has an expected value **not** copied from the DUT algorithm.

```cpp
// BAD — tautology / coverage-only
tb.check(true, "backdoor did not crash");
run_cmd(); /* no assertion */ PASS();
if (status == A || status == B || true) PASS();

// GOOD — independent, exact, fail-closed
EXPECT_EQ(trans.get_response_status(), tlm::TLM_ADDRESS_ERROR_RESPONSE);
EXPECT_EQ(rd(STATUS), ST_ERROR);          // not "timeout OR error"
EXPECT_EQ(claimed, 7u);                   // not dbg_claim_top()
```

Timeouts, “nonzero output”, and “completed” are not enough for crypto, DMA,
FIFO, or error paths. Use RDL/spec/NIST vectors or literal boundary tables.

## Mandatory TLM2.0 matrix (every target socket)

Issue raw `tlm_generic_payload` cases and assert **response + no mutation**
on rejects:

| Stimulus | Assert |
|---|---|
| READ/WRITE/IGNORE | exact status; IGNORE/reject leaves storage unchanged |
| null `data_ptr`, len 0 / 1 / width-1 / width+1 | no crash; documented status |
| unaligned addr, cross-window, hole, last byte | RAZ/WI vs `ADDRESS_ERROR` per contract |
| byte-enable + streaming_width 0 / &lt;len / &gt;len | merge/reject policy |
| incoming annotated delay | delay **observed** after transport (not only CCI set) |
| `transport_dbg` R/W | byte count + documented side-effect policy |
| DMI | `get_direct_mem_ptr` false or explicit grant; stale DMI flag cleared on error |

SMC: attach/monitor `smc::smc_axi_extension` on **outgoing** and incoming
filter/access decisions (`smc-axi-extension-canonical`). Do not fetch-and-ignore.

Negative benches **must** `sc_start` so threads (`transfer_thread`, timers)
actually run.

## Time, reset, concurrency

Do not `wait(long_time)` then sample. Assert at `T-ε`, `T`, `T+ε`, and
delta-cycle edges.

- Reset **asserted long enough** to cancel ticks, then deassert: prove the
  process rearms (CLINT-style stuck-timer).
- Reset during in-flight op: no stale VALID/IRQ/completion after release.
- Same-delta events: two engines, claim vs complete, FEED vs KEY, CTRL write
  during `wait(tick)`.
- Legal subword lanes (+1/+2/+4), FIFO full+1, max LEN vs buffer size.

If a test “expects” a surprising increment/completion, **stop and check the
model** — do not gold-file a bug.

## Coverage files

`coverage_*.cpp` / `*_cov_tb.cpp` are held to the same assertion bar.
No dummy backends whose outputs are then checked as “correct”. No offset
loops that only prove decode. No `GCOV_EXCL_*` for reachable code.

## Done

A new/changed bench is done only when: frontdoor cases exist for every
public socket/port/thread; TLM matrix is present; oracles are independent;
Release + `--asan` + `--coverage` all run the **same** suite; sanitizer logs
empty; ≥95% on touched model files from those genuine cases.
